{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Therefore, etc.</b> The sense: among his fat ones, the death of the great ones of Assyria, for so it is written:" "<b>יָקַד.</b> Like וַיֵּט שָׁמַיִם וַיֵּרַד (and He bowed the heavens and descended)." "<b>יוֹקַד.</b> On the pattern of כְּפוֹר (Psalm 147:17)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {2 "He cites a parallel for the root יקד (to burn/kindle); the point seems to concern the apocopated/shortened root form יקד analogous to ויט from נטה."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:13.303149700Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}